    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "For two terms, use the conjugate: same terms, opposite sign.\n\n2/(2+√2) uses 2−√2.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Multiply:\n\n2(2−√2) / [(2+√2)(2−√2)]\n= 2(2−√2)/(4−2)\n= 2−√2\n\nThe conjugate turns the denominator into a difference of squares.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
